Parent: 1444

## Context
Author clarification, 2026-11-07: the harness already repeats that not observed does not mean false. Diagnose failures in transcript evidence rather than adding another rule.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Harness-doctor retains an on-demand semantic diagnostic pairing a failed/unavailable observation with a subsequent claim of false, zero, absence, or all-clear; specify sample/window/runtime coverage and evidence limits.
- [ ] Controls distinguish an unsupported absence claim, a genuinely observed zero, and explicit unknown. A keyword hit or content-free digest alone is not a semantic verdict.
- [ ] Demonstrate a bounded authorized sample or report precisely why semantic inspection is unavailable. An empty audit is valid only for material actually inspected; never turn unavailable evidence into no finding.
- [ ] No new taxonomy rule, routine healthcheck, scheduled sweep, automatic classifier verdict, or merge-gate integration.
